    "docstring": "A mixin class that enforces user authentication before allowing access to a view. It's designed to be used with Django's class-based views to restrict access to logged-in users only.\n\nThis mixin checks if a user is authenticated. If not, it redirects the user to the login page. If the user *is* authenticated, it allows the view's `get` or `post` (or other HTTP methods) to proceed.\n\n**Inheritance:**\n\nThis class is intended to be mixed into other class-based views. It does *not* inherit from any base class itself, but is designed to be used with Django's `View` or its subclasses.\n\n**Attributes:**\n\n*   `login_url`: (str) The URL to redirect to if the user is not logged in. Defaults to `/accounts/login/`.\n*   `redirect_field_name`: (str) The query string parameter to use for redirecting the user back to the original page after login. Defaults to `next`.\n\n**Methods:**\n\n*   `dispatch(request, *args, **kwargs)`:  The core method that handles the authentication check. It overrides the `dispatch` method of the view it's mixed into.  It checks if the user is authenticated. If not, it redirects to the login page. If authenticated, it calls the parent class's `dispatch` method.\n\n**Example:**\n\n```python\nfrom django.views import View\nfrom django.contrib.auth.mixins import LoginRequiredMixin\n\nclass MyProtectedView(LoginRequiredMixin, View):\n    def get(self, request, *args, **kwargs):\n        # Your view logic here, accessible only to logged-in users\n        return HttpResponse(\"Hello, logged-in user!\")\n```\n\n**Raises:**\n\n*   `PermissionDenied`:  If the user is not authenticated and `raise_exception` is set to `True` (which is not a default behavior).",
